WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, welcome back.
We're here with Andy Samberg

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the cast,
Kenan Thompson, John Mulaney

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
and writers Colin Jost
and Rob Klein of tonight's

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.243 size:88% position:44%
"Second Chance Theater."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, Andy,
we'll start with you.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.079 line:92%
How do you feel it played?

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm feeling like I wish I had
changed before this part.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right, that you're still
in full Griff Banks,

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're still wearing the wig
-Yeah.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
Starting to regret that
a little bit.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mean it's hard
to get out of character.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You're so method about it

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-What did you just say to me

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:37.604
-Do you, Rob and Colin, do you
remember writing this sketch

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very well.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:43.510
-And did it sort of fly off --
fly onto the page, I should say?

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did the inspiration
just come fast and furious

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think
Griff kind of wrote it.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah,
Griff kind of wrote himself.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Griff wrote it for us.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-To dress twice.
Do you remember the two hosts?

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.725 line:92%
-Emma Stone and Gabourey Sidibe.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there you go.
-Right.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.062
-Yeah.
-Classic find-and-replace, yeah.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Did you -- Do you remember -

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.332
Well, you were in it both times.
Do you feel like it

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
played well enough to go to --
-I was in it both times?

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Nice.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.672 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, yeah, I loved it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.546 size:75% position:38%
Each and every time.
-John, you have some

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:23.083
other favorites of Andy's that
did not find their way to air.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.384 size:81% position:41%
Do you want to share
some of those with us?

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This wasn't on air?
Griff Banks?

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.187 size:81% position:41%
-This was never aired.
-Oh, it went to dress.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.955
-Yeah, it went to dress.
-Which is right before air

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Then they cut it.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:32.759 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We worked on a piece,
I think it was Friday nigh

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
till about 4:00 a.m.,
called --

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.265 line:92%
It was an "Update" feature

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did "Update."
-Yeah, I did, yeah, yeah.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was called
"The Guy Who Just Woke Up.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.705 size:88% position:44%
So Andy would come out,
and he'd be like, "Ahh."

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
He'd be tired, you know?
He just woke up.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.343
And I remember we got off
the elevator at 4:00 a.m.,

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.846
and we had turned it in,
and we were in the lobby.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we all wanted to go home
and Andy said, "Oh, wait.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe we should call him
Bedhead Jones."

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And...

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, we were like --
we were like, "I don't know.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bedhead Jones.
We kind of want to go home,"

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.293 line:92%
but looking back, I think that

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
that would've saved it."

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.264
-Yeah, I think it would've
Would've put it over the top

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I realize today
how many of your character

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:17.036
that we worked on had the entire
premise of the sketch

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the name of the character
-Right.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you got to let them know
up front.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All the jokes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.712 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There was Gerald.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gerald who's always sick.
Also cut.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, never aired.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gerard, the worse dude ever
also cut.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gerard, the worst dude ever
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember a couple thing
about Gerard?

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.523
Couple of details I remember
of Gerard, he rode in on a -

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do they call it?
Recumbent bike?

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Recumbent bike.
-Teva sandals.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Teva sandals.
-Tevas and socks.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:45.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He followed -- He was lik
a Deadhead but for Jamiroquai.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, the Quai.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
He followed the Quai.
-We referred to them as the --

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's on tour with the Quai.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He had an iguana
named Gary Larson.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.243
-Yep, creator of "The Far Side."
-Who was it that liked

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
Martinelli's
sparkling apple cider?

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was --
-I texted you on Thanksgiving.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We just
were talking about this.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Lomax.
-Lomax!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Lomax.
-None of these aired.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.525
-Can you do Lomax's voice for us
for a second?

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, and truly.
Such a pleasure to see you

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:16.796 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.832
Would you like another glass o
Martinelli's sparkling cider

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
